msgid "Tilt Rotor Setup Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:5
#: 4218698454b641d89bd6502a00921510
msgid "Tilt Rotor Planes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:7
#: 98dc5a707be743a3b355bf368901a79e
msgid "Tilt rotors are treated by ArduPilot as a special type of QuadPlane. You should start off by reading the :ref:`QuadPlane documentation <quadplane-support>` before moving onto this tilt-rotor specific documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:12
#: ddbbad40e897489088bb9998799af976
msgid "In ArduPilot nomenclature, a tilt-rotor is a type of VTOL aircraft where transition between hover and forward flight is accomplished by tilting one or more rotors so that it provides forward thrust instead of upward thrust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:17
#: 9a1e79c7e1ad43ffb9ffea91fd7f5614
msgid "This is distinct from :ref:`tailsitters <guide-tailsitter>` where the autopilot and main fuselage change orientation when moving between hover and forward flight. Do  not use the information below for a Tailsitter, some parameters are shared, but use the  instructions in the :ref:`guide-tailsitter`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:21
#: 333de0b9c99b482ea597ad5fb007f628
msgid "Types of Tilt-Rotors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:23
#: cc42b344326b4bce848eb6a16ef11f92
msgid "ArduPilot supports a very wide range of tilt-rotor configurations. Common configurations include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:26
#: c371a9d308194666907a6df78a80c96b
msgid "tilt-quadplanes with the front two motors tilting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:27
#: 06cd5d794e61470fa8a617461e03397a
msgid "tilt-quadplanes with all four motors tilting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:28
#: b95655bede4942f9863f4e50eaeb9614
msgid "tilt-tricopters with the front two motors tilting and rear tilt for yaw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:30
#: b68c673408a54c8ba9adf2c0eae5cc1e
msgid "tilt-tricopters with the front two motors tilting and vectored yaw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:31
#: da7b606a2f1745bda43781ab2f38c1df
msgid "tilt-hexacopters with the front four motors tilting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:32
#: 3da2240c37ea4898acdd5f4912eef188
msgid "tilt-wings where the main wing tilts along with two motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:33
#: fe202195523a45b2a805b9ad2b2725cd
msgid "binary-tiltrotors where the tilt mechanism can only be in one of two positions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:34
#: 4e047c515ce741e990763f7b4b405758
msgid "continuous-tiltrotors where the tilt mechanism can be controlled to any angle in a range from straight up to straight forward"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:36
#: 88cda4ab8db94cceacd5baf50741fb8f
msgid "vectored tilt-rotors where the tilt of the rotors on the left can be controlled independently from the tilt of the right motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:39
#: 19224bf5cf2d49faac8ff14f8e9c4634
msgid "Combined with these variants are versions that use ailerons, elevons, vtails and other control surfaces for fixed wing flight. There are an amazing number of combinations possible, and experimentation with VTOL designs is common. ArduPilot aims to support a very wide range of tilt-rotor configurations with a small number of parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:46
#: 917a0354d22841038a89761349d8ce39
msgid "Setting Up A Tilt-Rotor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:48
#: 5391eb3593e142ef878a77769a005dbf
msgid "The first thing you need to do is enable QuadPlane support by setting :ref:`Q_ENABLE<Q_ENABLE>` to 1 and Tilt Rotor support by setting :ref:`Q_TILT_ENABLE<Q_TILT_ENABLE>` = \"1\", and then choose the right quadplane frame class and frame type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:51
#: 45815c66330e4b359ca471dcb9497d46
msgid "The quadplane frame class is in :ref:`Q_FRAME_CLASS<Q_FRAME_CLASS>`. The frame class is chosen based on your vehicles rotor configuration while hovering. Currently supported tilt-rotor frame classes are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:70
#: cdff9cce468d4ad2bb08c3137cd2cb7b
msgid "Once you have chosen your frame class you will need to get the :ref:`Q_FRAME_TYPE<Q_FRAME_TYPE>` right. The :ref:`Q_FRAME_TYPE<Q_FRAME_TYPE>` is the sub-type of frame. For example, for a Quadcopter, a frame type of 1 is for a \"X\" frame and a frame type of 3 is for a \"H\" frame. For Tri and Y6, this parameter is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:75
#: b58e50a8160d4b0382ef433731529ca8
msgid "Please see the ArduCopter setup guide for multi-copters for more information on choosing your frame type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:78
#: 7a5a0ad8274a40aa98c4b42fbe300841
msgid "After setting up :ref:`Q_ENABLE<Q_ENABLE>`, :ref:`Q_FRAME_CLASS<Q_FRAME_CLASS>` and :ref:`Q_FRAME_TYPE<Q_FRAME_TYPE>` you will need to reboot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:82
#: ac98c2daddb84407af010b17abc7f506
msgid "The Tilt Mask"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:84
#: 5a8f64f4370d492c9d4eec018f9d655c
msgid "The most important parameter for a tilt-rotor is the tilt-mask, in the :ref:`Q_TILT_MASK<Q_TILT_MASK>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:87
#: 3a44ffa490d24792962781d1b2b699c7
msgid "The :ref:`Q_TILT_MASK<Q_TILT_MASK>` is a bitmask of what motors can tilt on your vehicle. The bits you need to enable correspond to the motor ordering of the standard ArduCopter motor map for your chosen frame class and frame type, ie. bit 0 corresponds to Motor 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:92
#: b2e177f6202a404596cb846199f2bb05
msgid "For example, if you have a tilt-tricopter where the front two motors tilt, then you should set :ref:`Q_TILT_MASK<Q_TILT_MASK>` to 3, which is 2+1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:95
#: f7d1e4a6de23486ab181ecf2ec4a72b7
msgid "If you have a tilt-quadplane where all 4 motors tilt, then you should set :ref:`Q_TILT_MASK<Q_TILT_MASK>` to 15, which is 8+4+2+1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:99
#: 4a7a8bf9b0d14eae90c335fd90840628
msgid "The Tilt Type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:101
#: 546198d56204413698f4aa99df17852e
msgid "Most tilt-rotors use normal servos for tilting their rotors. This allows the autopilot to control the angle of tilt continuously in a range from straight up to straight forward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:105
#: 924b352c36ee49678972d1d735db247d
msgid "Some tilt-rotors instead have a binary mechanism, typically using retract servos, where the autopilot can command the servo into either a fully up or fully forward position, but can't ask for the tilt to stop at some angle in between."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:110
#: e840625b86a9413899c7e1c9c48550d3
msgid "Finally some tilt-rotors have vectored control of yaw, where they can control yaw by tilting the left rotors independently of the right rotors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:114
#: 6340d97e01aa430e9e656c9ca01aa078
msgid "You need to set the type of tilt you have using the :ref:`Q_TILT_TYPE<Q_TILT_TYPE>` parameter. Valid values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:129
#: c999b89b00324024ab5eff169ef41ad9
msgid "Tilt Servos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:131
#: c3246d586b614040980272e561d63a0a
msgid "Next you need to configure which servo outputs will control tilt of the tiltable rotors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:134
#: 4d9d71500bd944c5856535c4f95411c7
msgid "You control that with the following servo function values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:148
#: a098c9b0e4674d03b5d2b50af0aae974
msgid "For Vectored Yaw applications, the right and left tilt servos would be used for front and/or back. You should choose normal ``TiltMotorsFront`` and/or ``TiltMotorsRear`` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:151
#: cf58f6e45fad4cceac7eaf56e7a09130
msgid "Tilt Reversal and Range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:153
#: fd9da211b872478ba4a7c64863a26bcb
msgid "You will need to set the ``SERVOn_REVERSED`` parameter on your tilt servos according to the direction of your servos. You should adjust so that in MANUAL mode the rotors are tilted forward and in QSTABILIZE mode they point straight up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:158
#: 88d17ad7f6614534b57ea1f2bf2409eb
msgid "You will probably also need to adjust the SERVOn_MIN an SERVOn_MAX values to adjust the range of movement and the exact angle of each servo for forward flight and hover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:163
#: 11ad52202e024d30a6aaf85c39fa3a68
msgid "Tilt Angle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:165
#: dedff6194dc74669a6d7f876a7f1a7c7
msgid "The :ref:`Q_TILT_MAX<Q_TILT_MAX>` parameter controls the tilt angle during transitions for continuous tilt vehicles. It is the angle in degrees that the rotors will move to while waiting for the transition airspeed to be reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:170
#: 2ef2b8e52fc74dd3b7fd461a731fda73
msgid "The right value for :ref:`Q_TILT_MAX<Q_TILT_MAX>` depends on how much tilt you need to achieve sufficient airspeed for the wings to provide most of the lift. For most tilt-rotors the default of 45 degrees is good."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:175
#: 55b57fdea6c24d6e93f057bc656f062c
msgid "Tilt Rate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:177
#: af3f9a720aa047409cff2b1427af78b1
msgid "A critical parameter for tilt rotors is how quickly they move the tilt servos when transitioning between hover and forward flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:180
#: 908258cd3bf9420ab380500b1b59ed7a
msgid "The two parameters that control tilt rate are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:182
#: 56685dd5fe584aac970856f4309b4229
msgid ":ref:`Q_TILT_RATE_UP<Q_TILT_RATE_UP>` is the tilt rate upwards in degrees per second"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:183
#: 54e51d5e3c2d41b18983c05c47708114
msgid ":ref:`Q_TILT_RATE_DN<Q_TILT_RATE_DN>` is the tilt rate downwards in degrees per second"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:185
#: 48334f79f6a64086a35e4c73c0d2b59f
msgid "If :ref:`Q_TILT_RATE_DN<Q_TILT_RATE_DN>` is zero then :ref:`Q_TILT_RATE_UP<Q_TILT_RATE_UP>` is used for both directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:188
#: 750e28039f2d4b3e8406d57141a28f58
msgid "How fast you should move the tilt servos depends on a number of factors, particularly on how well tuned your vehicle is for multi-rotor flight. In general it is recommended to err on the side of slow transitions for initial testing, then slowly speed it up as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:194
#: 3daa9f46ea634cb2989a236fe8078dd7
msgid "A typical value would be 15 degrees per second for both up and down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:196
#: 2252e27996c449c0be4d40bf0da9732b
msgid "Note that there are some automatic exceptions to the tilt rate in the ArduPilot tilt-rotor code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:199
#: 340c259893e84d6bbb2d779e7ddfd79b
msgid "the tilt rate when changing to MANUAL mode is 90 degrees per second. This gives you rapid forward flight control in case MANUAL mode is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:203
#: 2b2a74cf432d4d359aafedd1689299f3
msgid "once a forward transition is completed then the motors will cover any remaining angle at 90 degrees per second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:206
#: c70897a3c8f94ff8b8659a96eecc5982
msgid "For Binary type tilt servos these rates should be set at the actual measured rate of the servo since it's independent of ArduPilot control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:209
#: e5e613b5382543a8a2571015a16f07ac
msgid "Tilt Stabilization Assist in Fixed Wing Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:211
#: a1e5884b4dd640808626edbaa1213512
msgid "It is possible to use the tilt motors (if not the BINARY tilt type) to aid in fixed wing roll and pitch control. This is activated if the :ref:`Q_TILT_FIX_GAIN<Q_TILT_FIX_GAIN>` is greater than zero, which determines how much control demand results in tilting of the motors. The maximum tilt angle achievable is determined by the :ref:`Q_TILT_FIX_ANGLE<Q_TILT_FIX_ANGLE>` parameter. It is recommended to start with 0.1 for the :ref:`Q_TILT_FIX_GAIN<Q_TILT_FIX_GAIN>` and work your way up to desired the response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:213
#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:235
#: b6ae76bb80f740d39dd10e5b93dea70c
#: f2772fd8fc9c44f89ade8ee7e6080dd3
msgid "In order to setup the ranges of the servo movement, see :ref:`tilt-rotor-setup`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:216
#: edc7078a633e4b9283c3a1dd1120c95f
msgid "Vectored Yaw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:218
#: cd61bf07cd5a404b90c753b586a23e0c
msgid "Vectored yaw aircraft tilt the left and right rotors (front and/or rear, if used) separately to control yaw in hover. This reduces mechanical complexity in tilt-tricopters as it avoids the need for a tilt servo for the rear motor for yaw control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:223
#: 9db711a593b14b5483781ed65e2a1785
msgid "To setup a vectored yaw aircraft you need to set :ref:`Q_TILT_TYPE<Q_TILT_TYPE>` =2, and also set :ref:`Q_TILT_YAW_ANGLE<Q_TILT_YAW_ANGLE>` to the angle in degrees that the tilt motors can go up past 90 degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:227
#: 8232a5089314401e82c435edb91b7d21
msgid "For example, if you have a tilt-tricopter with vectored yaw, and your front motors can tilt through a total of 110 degrees from forward flight, then your :ref:`Q_TILT_YAW_ANGLE<Q_TILT_YAW_ANGLE>` would be 20, as that is the angle past 90 degrees that the tilt mechanism can go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:232
#: 057c952756b94ba7954a722cbd41441d
msgid "You also need to setup your two tilt servos with ``SERVOn_FUNCTION`` =75 for left front tilt and ``SERVOn_FUNCTION`` =76 for right front tilt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:238
#: 15f7fa216eb54a239dacc30438bf7761
msgid "Non-Vectored Yaw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:240
#: f77e2a3841564513be176c236a8b9e70
msgid "Non-Vectored yaw aircraft (:ref:`Q_TILT_TYPE<Q_TILT_TYPE>` = 0 or 1) needs a tilt servo for yaw control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:242
#: 44f908892bfb45f7a0baec0006d64274
msgid "You need to setup your front tilt servos with ``SERVOn_FUNCTION=41`` and also your servo for yaw control with ``SERVOn_FUNCTION=39``, if the frame is a Tricopter. You should set up the yaw servo’s maximum lean angle in degrees with :ref:`Q_M_YAW_SV_ANGLE<Q_M_YAW_SV_ANGLE>`. This lean angle assumes that ``SERVOn_MIN`` and ``SERVOn_MAX``, represent +/- 90 degrees, with ``SERVOn_TRIM`` representing 0 degrees lean."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:244
#: 5c6adb1ebd2849119c033a30aff8c4d1
msgid "Note: ``SERVO_FUNCTION=39`` is normally the output function for motor 7, but in a non-vectored yaw tilt-rotor Tricopter, the yaw servo is controlled via ``SERVOn_FUNCTION`` = 39."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:247
#: c1819223fcbb4b72bbb9edad1a2a142f
msgid "If you wish to setup BLEHeli esc telemetry, you need to set :ref:`Q_M_PWM_TYPE<Q_M_PWM_TYPE>` to 4 (DShot 150), connect the telemetry signal to a SERIAL port, and set its ``SERIALn_PROTOCOL`` to 23."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:249
#: edc7a198c1e84ec3b5b59bcb7cdd5c16
msgid "Note that if you want to use BLHeli passthru setup or telemetry in a non-vectored yaw Tricopter, you must not set :ref:`SERVO_BLH_AUTO<SERVO_BLH_AUTO>` to 1. Instead, set :ref:`SERVO_BLH_MASK<SERVO_BLH_MASK>` to the output-bitmask of the servo-channels actually connected BLHELI-ESCs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:253
#: f700deef6a454eb5864641b340938952
msgid "For example if your motors are connected to servo 9,10,11 (the first three aux-outputs of a pixhawk1), set :ref:`SERVO_BLH_MASK<SERVO_BLH_MASK>` to 1792."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:258
#: 8cc8724be3e841f988908139c13953e4
msgid "BiCopter Tilt-Rotor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:260
#: 69673547ffb84ef6bd056b66245a2af0
msgid "This is a special case of tilt-rotor QuadPlane. Setup is a bit different, but the configuration is actually a normal QuadPlane and performs QuadPlane transitions. In order to setup this vehicle configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:262
#: 983e8e406449452d950641762acec4f6
msgid ":ref:`Q_FRAME_CLASS<Q_FRAME_CLASS>` = 10 (Tailsitter, even though this is not a tailsitter!)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:263
#: 984c6c3c47554857ae6651c5dab62721
msgid ":ref:`Q_TILT_TYPE<Q_TILT_TYPE>` = 3 (BiCopter)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:266
#: 372cd538ec5746eabb93966298ee29ba
msgid "Motor and Tilt Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:268
#: 83d935d1139f43289d4d31d6081b81a5
msgid "For motors and tilt servos,you should set the SERVOn_FUNCTION values for your two tilt servos for the left and right motors, and for the left and right motor throttles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:270
#: 003c1103a1f54149a903ffeecbbe6676
msgid "The tilt servo limits are setup a bit differently than other Tilt Rotors. To setup, a normal tilt rotor range, you would set the :ref:`Q_TILT_YAW_ANGLE<Q_TILT_YAW_ANGLE>`, then the tilt servo's MIN and MAX output range to get vertical in QSTABLIZE and horizontal in MANUAL on the bench.The TRIM value is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:272
#: 0e286eecfd7546038706e2ff568e64cf
msgid "With this frame type, the tilt servo's MIN sets horizontal position, TRIM the vertical position, and MAX the full rearward (max  VTOL yaw). In this case, the user must set the :ref:`Q_TILT_YAW_ANGLE<Q_TILT_YAW_ANGLE>` for the amount of forward yaw from vertical (should match the rearward angle to prevent asymmetric yaw authority in one direction)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:274
#: 2d6f6369800d4d109ef9cdb445a4a2cf
msgid "MIN and MAX may be swapped if the tilt servo had to be reversed to get proper directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:276
#: cbaf2d4f22c04a869fff378de2ecba14
msgid "Otherwise, this frame type conforms to the normal vectored yaw tilt-rotor QuadPlane transitions, and parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:279
#: a39e702aa5344832b11c4b824ddc753d
msgid "Tilt Rotor Movement Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:286
#: 56a6d233256e4305b846d8ed22112a13
msgid "Also:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:287
#: 9dfb636cef1f47a19d2e9297a2dfa870
msgid ":ref:`Tilt Rotor Servo Setup<tilt-rotor-setup>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:290
#: 14ceaeac42984ae79d7e385ce3d6757d
msgid "Tilt Wing Flap Emulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:292
#: 855e184ca9d1459187f32cac61b290a4
msgid "Tilt Wing Tilt Rotors are where the entire wing rotates, instead of the motors. These frames use the \"TiltMotorsFront\" ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` (41) to tilt the entire wing for fixed-wing or VTOL operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:294
#: 34da7fc2b62e47178a8b57f51a98a453
msgid "You can  also set up the wing to tilt just like (or in addition to) normal manually controlled or :ref:`automaticflaps <automatic-flaps>`, and the wing will tilt in fixed wing modes just as a flap would activate. The amount of wing tilt when flaps are fully extended is set by the :ref:`Q_TILT_WING_FLAP<Q_TILT_WING_FLAP>` parameter to tilt the wing up to 15 degrees when full flaps are activated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:297
#: f1ba6e0f2cbb420c9d683721a5921ce5
msgid "Pre Flight Checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/guide-tilt-rotor.rst:299
#: da9096ac628549678aebb923273b4c43
msgid "In addition to the normal pre-flight checks for a QuadPlane, you should check your tilt-rotor transition by changing between MANUAL and QSTABILIZE modes on the ground. Make sure that your tilt moves smoothly and that the servos are trimmed correctly for the right rotor angles."
msgstr ""
